From: (unattributed — take it as a suggestion, not a claim of authorship)
Subject: [PATCH] io: do not assert on an unfilled msg_name from recvmsg

`recvmsg` fills `msg_name` only for an unconnected socket. On a connected one the
kernel sets `msg_namelen = 0` and leaves the buffer alone, so the family byte read
back in `zioIpToStdIo` is whatever was on the stack, and the `else` branch is
reached. `netReceiveImpl` (src/io.zig:2406) and `extractBatchResult`
(src/io.zig:865) both convert unconditionally, which is why this is fixed in the
conversion rather than at either call site.

`std.Io.Threaded` leaves the same storage `undefined` (std/Io/Threaded.zig:13092)
and is fine because its `addressFromPosix` defines the case away
(std/Io/Threaded.zig:14176-14183). zio's own accept path already does the same
thing (src/io.zig:1948-1953).

Rationale and evidence: zio-net-receive.md next to this file.
---
 src/io.zig | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/io.zig b/src/io.zig
index 3296829..5a671c3 100644
--- a/src/io.zig
+++ b/src/io.zig
@@ -1827,7 +1827,10 @@ fn zioIpToStdIo(addr: zio_net.IpAddress) Io.net.IpAddress {
             .flow = addr.in6.flowinfo,
             .interface = .{ .index = addr.in6.scope_id },
         } },
-        else => unreachable,
+        // recvmsg leaves msg_name untouched on a connected socket, so the family
+        // read back here can be whatever was on the stack. Matches
+        // std.Io.Threaded's addressFromPosix, which returns this same placeholder.
+        else => .{ .ip4 = .loopback(0) },
     };
 }
 
